{"id":"bond-projects","title":"Bond-funded work: budget and finish date at the start and now","question":"Which parts of the voter-approved bond programmes are more than a quarter over their bond allocation or two years past their first finish date?","finding":"Of 71 bond components in the Controller's reports, 33 are two years or more past the finish date first given (40 a year or more) and 1 has a bond budget a quarter or more above the amount first allocated; 33 meet one test or the other, with bond budgets of $2.20 billion. The latest: Final Design (65%) (Embarcadero Seawall Earthquake Safety (2018)), first due 2024-04-05 and now 2035-12-31 (not finished). Between the two reports on file (FY22-23 and FY24-25), 23 components moved their finish date back by six months or more. The project list counts 7,644 planned projects or housing units, 3,693 of them complete, and 49 entries with a completion date still ahead. No bond file names the builder, so none of this can be set against a contractor.","how":"The Controller's bond programme table gives, for each component of each bond, the amount of bond money first allocated, the revised bond budget, money spent, the finish date first projected for the last project in it, and the projected or actual finish date. The latest report for each component (FY24-25 where there is one) is used, and the earlier report shows what moved in between. Months late is the present or actual finish date less the first; over is the revised bond budget against the first allocation. Oversight and issuance lines are left out. An earlier file in this project (the “late screens” results) lists the components a year or more late with budgets of $5 million or more; this screen adds the budget test, the movement between the two reports and the count of projects.","limits":"These are bond dollars only: the amount voters authorized for the component, the revised bond budget and what has been spent. A revised bond budget above the first allocation means bond money was moved into the component, and the table does not say from where; a project's whole budget, with its other funds, is not in this table. The capital-project budget and schedule reports are the record for that. A component is a group of projects and, by the table's own definition, its finish date is that of the last project in it, so one late project makes a whole component late. Components that fund housing or grants depend on other parties' schedules. The table is updated every two years, so the latest figures are already old.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"program","t":"Bond","type":"text"},{"k":"component","t":"Component","type":"text"},{"k":"authorized","t":"Bond money first allocated","type":"usd"},{"k":"budget","t":"Bond budget now","type":"usd"},{"k":"over","t":"Over the first allocation","type":"pct"},{"k":"spent","t":"Spent","type":"usd"},{"k":"spentShare","t":"Share spent","type":"pct"},{"k":"originalEnd","t":"First finish date","type":"date"},{"k":"nowEnd","t":"Finish date now","type":"date"},{"k":"finished","t":"Status","type":"text"},{"k":"monthsLate","t":"Months late","type":"int"},{"k":"slip","t":"Months slipped since the earlier report","type":"int"},{"k":"budgetChange","t":"Bond budget change since the earlier report","type":"usd"},{"k":"asOf","t":"Report","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"program":"Embarcadero Seawall Earthquake Safety (2018)","component":"Final Design (65%)","authorized":162000000,"budget":162000000,"over":0.0,"spent":621324,"spentShare":0.004,"originalEnd":"2024-04-05","nowEnd":"2035-12-31","finished":"not finished","monthsLate":141,"slip":120,"asOf":"FY24-25"},{"program":"Embarcadero Seawall Earthquake Safety (2018)","component":"Planning/Engineering/Preliminary Design (35%)","authorized":61000000,"budget":61000000,"over":0.0,"spent":34338317,"spentShare":0.563,"originalEnd":"2023-01-05","nowEnd":"2032-12-31","finished":"not finished","monthsLate":120,"slip":108,"asOf":"FY24-25"},{"program":"Clean & Safe Neighborhood